-</pre></section><section class="tab" id="tab-search"><h3 class="tabname">Search</h3><table class='kv'><tr><th>Records retrieved</th><td>120</td></tr><tr><th>Databases / sources</th><td>PubMed, ClinicalTrials.gov</td></tr><tr><th>Committed cache</th><td>cache/colchicine-secondary-cv-prevention/records.json</td></tr><tr><th>Run (UTC)</th><td>2026-09-11</td></tr></table><h4>Retrieval snapshot</h4><div class='banner'><p><strong>Snapshot:</strong> records_sha256 <code>2d3b2a35</code>; retrieved_utc 2026-09-11; mode LEGACY_UNRECORDED: a pre-ledger fetch; which query retrieved which record was not recorded; every record's found_by names this single source.</p><p>This page replays the committed retrieval snapshot; it is not a claim that the protocol SHA alone regenerates the page byte-for-byte. A live re-search is a separate, dated event (see Re-search below if present).</p></div><h4>Retrieval sources</h4><table class='recs'><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Query</th><th>Run date</th><th>State</th><th>hits -&gt; fetched -&gt; retained</th><th>Cap</th><th>Discovery-capable</th></tr><tr><td>PUBMED_LEGACY_QUERY</td><td><code>&quot;Efficacy and Safety of Low-Dose Colchicine after Myocardial Infarction&quot;</code></td><td>2026-09-11</td><td><strong>RAN_UNRECORDED</strong>: attempted by a pre-ledger fetch; its yield was never recorded, so neither a count nor a zero can be shown (legacy only — a live run may not carry this state)</td><td>unknown -&gt; 0 -&gt; 0</td><td>none (n=unknown; remainder=unknown)</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td>PUBMED_LEGACY_QUERY</td><td><code>&quot;Colchicine in Patients with Chronic Coronary Disease&quot;</code></td><td>2026-09-11</td><td><strong>RAN_UNRECORDED</strong>: attempted by a pre-ledger fetch; its yield was never recorded, so neither a count nor a zero can be shown (legacy only — a live run may not carry this state)</td><td>unknown -&gt; 0 -&gt; 0</td><td>none (n=unknown; remainder=unknown)</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td>PUBMED_LEGACY_QUERY</td><td><code>colchicine coronary disease placebo randomized double-blind</code></td><td>2026-09-11</td><td><strong>RAN_UNRECORDED</strong>: attempted by a pre-ledger fetch; its yield was never recorded, so neither a count nor a zero can be shown (legacy only — a live run may not carry this state)</td><td>unknown -&gt; 0 -&gt; 0</td><td>none (n=unknown; remainder=unknown)</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td>LEGACY_UNRECORDED</td><td><code>&quot;Efficacy and Safety of Low-Dose Colchicine after Myocardial Infarction&quot; || &quot;Colchicine in Patients with Chronic Coronary Disease&quot; || colchicine coronary disease placebo randomized double-blind</code></td><td>2026-09-11</td><td><strong>RAN_OK</strong>: ran and returned records</td><td>unknown -&gt; 95 -&gt; 95</td><td>none (n=unknown; remainder=unknown)</td><td>no</td></tr></table><h4>Source status (which adapters ran)</h4><p class='muted'>Citation chase: <strong>NOT_RUN</strong> · ClinicalTrials.gov: <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · Europe PMC (OA + metadata): <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · Legacy unrecorded retrieval: <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · PMC full text: <strong>NOT_RUN</strong> · PubMed: <strong>RAN_OK</strong> · Registry-first (AACT): <strong>RAN_OK</strong> — RAN_OK = ran and returned records; RAN_ZERO = ran, none matched; RAN_ERROR = attempted but failed; NOT_RUN = not attempted for this topic.</p><h4>Retrieval class</h4><div class='absent'><p><strong>TITLE-SEEDED RETRIEVAL — DISCOVERY-BIASED, NOT A SYSTEMATIC SEARCH</strong> We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic. an auditable screening ledger attached to an unauditable retrieval process.</p></div><table class='recs'><tr><th>Verbatim query</th><th>Kind</th><th>Features fired</th></tr><tr><td><code>&quot;Efficacy and Safety of Low-Dose Colchicine after Myocardial Infarction&quot;</code></td><td>NAME_SEEDED</td><td>trial_acronym_token:Low-Dose</td></tr><tr><td><code>&quot;Colchicine in Patients with Chronic Coronary Disease&quot;</code></td><td>FREE_TEXT_KEYWORD</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><code>colchicine coronary disease placebo randomized double-blind</code></td><td>FREE_TEXT_KEYWORD</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><code>&quot;Efficacy and Safety of Low-Dose Colchicine after Myocardial Infarction&quot; || &quot;Colchicine in Patients with Chronic Coronary Disease&quot; || colchicine coronary disease placebo randomized double-blind</code></td><td>NAME_SEEDED</td><td>trial_acronym_token:Low-Dose</td></tr></table><div class='absent'><strong>Search provenance — not a completed systematic search.</strong> The registry-first (AACT) adapter status for this topic is <strong>RAN_OK</strong>; its evidence set was assembled by TITLE-SEEDED RETRIEVAL (title/name-anchored queries for pre-identified trials), which cannot discover an unknown eligible trial. A query seeded with the names of known trials is not a systematic search. We retract any claim of a registry-first or systematic search for this topic.</div><h4>Positive-control recovery (NOT systematic-review recall)</h4><p>Positive-control recovery: the committed registry query re-found <strong>2/3</strong> of this topic's PRE-SPECIFIED known trials (pooled + declared positive controls; enumerated 59; status RAN_OK). 1 missed trial(s) have <strong>no own-publication registry linkage</strong> — unregistered / pre-registration-era, so unreachable by any registry-first search (a property of the literature, not a search failure). <span class='muted'>Missed: 34876021.</span> <span class='muted'>Measured 2026-09-11T23:39:14Z.</span> <strong>This is not systematic-review recall.</strong> It measures whether the committed registry query re-finds the trials ALREADY KNOWN to the build; a trial that was never in the known set is not in the denominator, so a high value does <strong>not</strong> mean the search is complete ? external audits found eligible trials (J-EMPHASIS-HF, an eplerenone trial, for the MRA topic published under the identifier spironolactone-hfref-mortality, PHILO for ticagrelor) entirely absent precisely because they were never in a known set. True recall needs an INDEPENDENTLY-GENERATED reference universe (concept query + registry enumeration, not the seed list); that rebuild is in progress. Recovery is also search REACH, not inclusion — whether a recovered trial is eligible/poolable is the screen's and extractor's job.</p><h4>Registry landscape &amp; unpublished evidence (AACT)</h4><p>Of <strong>59</strong> registry records matching the query (broad — reach, not precision): 27 have a linked publication; <strong>0</strong> have posted CT.gov results but no publication (<em>poolable unpublished data no published meta in this topic has</em>); 6 are completed &ge;12 months ago with neither results nor a linked publication — a <em>loose upper bound</em> on non-publication, inflated by the broad enumeration and by NCT&rarr;PMID linkage misses, not a publication-bias claim. <span class='muted'>AACT 2026-08-30 (local snapshot).</span></p><h4>PubMed</h4><pre class='query'>&quot;Efficacy and Safety of Low-Dose Colchicine after Myocardial Infarction&quot;</pre><pre class='query'>&quot;Colchicine in Patients with Chronic Coronary Disease&quot;</pre><pre class='query'>colchicine coronary disease placebo randomized double-blind</pre><h4>ClinicalTrials.gov</h4><pre class='query'>{&quot;cond&quot;: &quot;coronary artery disease&quot;, &quot;intr&quot;: &quot;colchicine&quot;}</pre></section><section class="tab" id="tab-screening"><h3 class="tabname">Screening</h3><p class='muted'><strong>Identifier scope:</strong> identifier names colchicine; all included records map to that agent. Verdict: <code>MATCH</code>.</p><h4>Study selection flow (PRISMA 2020)</h4><table class='recs'><tr><th>Stage</th><th>n</th></tr><tr><td>Records identified (committed search)</td><td>120</td></tr><tr><td>Records screened (deduplicated)</td><td>120</td></tr><tr><td>Excluded at screening — by rule</td><td>95 (X-CONTRAST 1 · X-DEDUP 2 · X1 58 · X2 20 · X3 14)</td></tr><