g> mean the search is complete ? external audits found eligible trials (J-EMPHASIS-HF, an eplerenone trial, for the MRA topic published under the identifier spironolactone-hfref-mortality, PHILO for ticagrelor) entirely absent precisely because they were never in a known set. True recall needs an INDEPENDENTLY-GENERATED reference universe (concept query + registry enumeration, not the seed list); that rebuild is in progress. Recovery is also search REACH, not inclusion — whether a recovered trial is eligible/poolable is the screen's and extractor's job.</p><h4>Registry landscape &amp; unpublished evidence (AACT)</h4><p>Of <strong>95</strong> registry records matching the query (broad — reach, not precision): 39 have a linked publication; <strong>3</strong> have posted CT.gov results but no publication (<em>poolable unpublished data no published meta in this topic has</em>); 27 are completed &ge;12 months ago with neither results nor a linked publication — a <em>loose upper bound</em> on non-publication, inflated by the broad enumeration and by NCT&rarr;PMID linkage misses, not a publication-bias claim. <span class='muted'>AACT 2026-08-30 (local snapshot).</span></p><h4>PubMed</h4><pre class='query'>Dexamethasone[Title] Covid-19[Title] randomized controlled trial mortality usual care</pre><pre class='query'>Hydrocortisone[Title] COVID-19[Title] randomized clinical trial mortality</pre><pre class='query'>Metcovid methylprednisolone hospitalized COVID-19 randomized placebo mortality</pre><h4>ClinicalTrials.gov</h4><pre class='query'>{&quot;cond&quot;: &quot;COVID-19&quot;, &quot;intr&quot;: &quot;dexamethasone&quot;}</pre></section><section class="tab" id="tab-screening"><h3 class="tabname">Screening</h3><p class='muted'><strong>Identifier scope:</strong> identifier leading token matches class term corticosteroids. Verdict: <code>NOT_APPLICABLE</code>.</p><h4>Study selection flow (PRISMA 2020)</h4><table class='recs'><tr><th>Stage</th><th>n</th></tr><tr><td>Records ide