ble></div></section><section class="tab" id="tab-harms"><h3 class="tabname">Harms</h3><div class="absent"><strong>DECLARED ABSENT.</strong> no harms recorded</div></section><section class="tab" id="tab-comparator"><h3 class="tabname">Comparator</h3><table class='kv'><tr><th>Published comparator</th><td>SGLT2 inhibitors among patients with heart failure with preserved ejection fraction: A meta-analysis of randomised controlled trials. (2023), Medicine (Baltimore)</td></tr><tr><th>Identifier</th><td>PMID 37773799</td></tr><tr><th>Open access</th><td>True</td></tr><tr><th>URL</th><td>https://doi.org/10.1097/MD.0000000000034693</td></tr></table><h4>Scope match (is this the same question?)</h4><p><strong>⚠ SCOPE MISMATCH.</strong> Intervention level: topic is a single agent, comparator is class-level (match: False); population match: True. comparator is a DRUG-CLASS meta-analysis while this topic is a single agent — a PICO scope mismatch (single-drug review vs class-level review); the k difference vs this comparator is a scope difference, not unretrieved evidence <span class='muted'>Decided by one uniform rule applied to every topic before the k was seen.</span></p><p><strong>Comparator resolution.</strong> k=1 CONTRIBUTING, not a complete-evidence claim: EMPEROR-Preserved (NCT03057951) supplies the only EXTRACTABLE primary-outcome estimate here. This is NOT a claim that the eligible evidence base is a single trial -- 4 records screened in and 3 are declared absent for this pooled number. External audit identified EMPA-VISION (a randomised double-blind trial with a separate HFpEF cohort) as eligible and missed by the trial-level search; the cohort-level screening + concept-query rebuild is the fix. The nearest published synthesis pools the SGLT2-inhibitor CLASS (a broader, network-level PICO), so its larger k is a scope difference, not evidence this review failed to retrieve.</p><p>Legacy comparator extraction, theirs_k: not stated in the comparator abstract/full text.</