</td><td><strong>not stated (abstract only - full text not retrieved)</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td>abstract</td><td><strong>abstract</strong>: </td></tr><tr><td>PMID 38184150</td><td><strong>not stated (abstract only - full text not retrieved)</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td>abstract</td><td><strong>abstract</strong>: </td></tr><tr><td>NCT01048502</td><td><strong>source not retrieved</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td></td><td><strong></strong>: </td></tr><tr><td>NCT01841944</td><td><strong>source not retrieved</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td></td><td><strong></strong>: </td></tr><tr><td>NCT06720662</td><td><strong>source not retrieved</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td></td><td><strong></strong>: </td></tr></table></div><p><strong>Registry-machine-signal-restricted partial machine assessment</strong> (per pooled trial) &mdash; NOT a formal human risk-of-bias assessment, which requires human judgements the registry cannot supply. These are computed from what is machine-available (AACT 2026-08-30 + registry-vs-pooled (D5)). <strong>Domain 5 (selective reporting)</strong> is computed from the trial's REGISTERED primary outcome vs the outcome we pooled — a machine-checkable signal most published meta-analyses do not report. D1/D2/D4 use AACT structured allocation/masking fields. <strong>D3 (missing outcome data) is NOT ASSESSED for any trial — a stated limitation, not a per-trial judgement</strong>: the harness has no outcome-missingness evidence source (study discontinuation is not outcome missingness), so D3 is structurally unassessable here and is never rated; the attrition figures are shown as context only. This caps overall GRADE certainty below <em>high</em> corpus-wide (a required bias domain is unassessed), and it would be fixed by a committed outcome-missingness source (AACT <code>milestones</code> / the publication's flow diagram: analysed-vs-randomised at the outcome). Other risk-of-bias judgements that need human reading are likewise marked <em>not assessed</em>: partial-but-honest, never guessed. Hover a cell for its basis.</p><table class='recs'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Overall</th><th>D1 randomisation</th><th>D2 deviations/blinding</th><th>D3 missing data</th><th>D4 measurement</th><th>D5 selective reporting</th></tr><tr><td>20929341</td><td><strong>some concerns</strong></td><td title='AACT allocation = RANDOMIZED'>low</td><td title='trial masking = Quadruple (blinded): participants/personnel blinded'>low</td><td title='no AACT participant-flow data; outcome missingness needs human judgement'>not assessed</td><td title='trial masking = Quadruple (blinded): outcome assessment blinded'>low</td><td title='the pooled outcome matches no registered primary or secondary outcome (registered primary: &#x27;Major cardiovascular events, which comprises fatal cardiovascular diseases (CVD)&#x27;) -- possibly post-hoc/unregistered'>some concerns</td></tr><tr><td>21115589</td><td><strong>low (on assessed domains; some domains require human judgement)</strong></td><td title='AACT allocation = unstated'>not assessed</td><td title='the trial&#x27;s own abstract/text (double-blind/placebo-controlled) (blinded): participants/personnel blinded'>low</td><td title='no AACT participant-flow data; outcome missingness needs human judgement'>not assessed</td><td title='the trial&#x27;s own abstract/text (double-blind/placebo-controlled) (blinded): outcome assessment blinded'>low</td><td title='no registered primary or secondary outcomes available for this trial'>not_assessable</td></tr><tr><td>22686415</td><td><strong>low (on assessed domains; some domains require human judgement)</strong></td><td title='AACT allocation = RANDOMIZED'>low</td><td title='the trial&#x27;s own abstract/text (double-blind/placebo-controlled) (blinded): participants/personnel blinded'>low</td><td title='not assessed - AACT flow shows between-arm differential attrition 19.3% (overall 9.7%), but study discontinuation is NOT outcome missingness and outcome-dependence