esults_unavailable</span><br><span class='muted'>completeness basis: publication record / committed cache metadata</span><br><code>NOT_RETRIEVED</code></td></tr><tr><td>DIAMOND</td><td>NCT03190694</td><td class='absent-cell'>HM: source not retrieved</td><td>no percentage-corroborated arm counts or effect+CI for this outcome found in the abstract<br><code>SOURCE_NOT_RETRIEVED</code><br><span class='muted'>reason-code audit: <code>NOT_VERIFIABLE</code></span><br><span class='muted'>basis: SOURCE_NOT_RETRIEVED: cached abstract text is missing for this record</span><br><span class='muted'>completeness: eligible+completed+results_available</span><br><span class='muted'>completeness basis: publication record / committed cache metadata</span><br><code>NOT_RETRIEVED</code></td></tr></table></section><section class="tab" id="tab-comparator"><h3 class="tabname">Comparator</h3><table class='kv'><tr><th>Published comparator</th><td>SGLT2 Inhibitors and Kidney Outcomes by Glomerular Filtration Rate and Albuminuria: A Meta-Analysis. (2026), JAMA</td></tr><tr><th>Identifier</th><td>PMID 41203232</td></tr><tr><th>Open access</th><td>True</td></tr><tr><th>URL</th><td>https://doi.org/10.1001/jama.2025.20834</td></tr></table><h4>Scope match (is this the same question?)</h4><p><strong>⚠ SCOPE MISMATCH.</strong> Intervention level: topic is class-level, comparator is class-level (match: True); population match: True. SMART-C is a broader IPD consortium: seven of ten trials are CV/HF populations excluded by this CKD-progression protocol; the result supports the effect direction but is not a same-scope comparator. <span class='muted'>Decided by one uniform rule applied to every topic before the k was seen.</span></p><p>Legacy comparator extraction, shared_k: not exactly verifiable (comparator trial table not machine-exposed).</p><h3>Comparator panel</h3><p>MEASURED: overlaps use the live trial families for each outcome and strand. Unknown endpoint compatibility is not counted as compatible.</p><article data-comparator='41203232'><h4>SGLT2 Inhibitors and Kidney Outcomes by Glomerular Filtration Rate and Albuminuria: A Meta-Analysis. (2026); JAMA; DOI 10.1001/jama.2025.20834; PMID 41203232</h4><p>Registered comparator identity; unextracted quantities and trial membership remain unknown.</p><p>HELD: cache/sglt2-ckd-progression/comparator_fulltext.txt; SHA-256 369252fd522db6abddbaaf32177c5bd5603f6b9b671e39dc7f68d126ca38b9a5</p><dl><dt>k</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd><dt>effect</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd><dt>ci</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd><dt>i2</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd><dt>pi</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd><dt>method</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd></dl><p>Trial set NOT ENUMERATED; overlap unknown.</p></article></section><section class="tab" id="tab-riskofbias"><h3 class="tabname">Risk of bias</h3><p><strong>Coverage: 3 of 3 primary-outcome pooled trials assessed</strong> (3 from registry (AACT) + trial text)</p><div class='banner'><strong>RoB spans span-checked (cross-family): 97% agreement</strong> (32 of 33 scoreable), from a seeded sample of 45 model/registry-derived domain ratings independently checked by a different model family (Fable) against each trial abstract; 12 were unscoreable (no claim, or a conservative not-stated rating). This check itself found and fixed a real error &mdash; one trial (EMPHASIS-HF) was mislabelled NON_RANDOMIZED by the registry, contradicted by its abstract; the RoB block was also visibly broken until a human review caught it. The number is here because a RoB block a reader cannot trust is worthless (<code>docs/rob_spancheck.json</code>).</div><div class='absent'><strong>Parser-confirmed contrast disclosure (per pooled trial, from the AACT arm-label parser - disclosed, not an adjustment).</strong> This measures the parser, not the trial. Eligibility should test what actually DIFFERS between the randomised arms, not the mere presence of the drug word: a trial giving the drug of interest as BACKGROUND in every arm (e.g. all arms on the same agent, randomising a different drug) is not a randomised comparison of it. For each pooled trial the randomised contrast is reconstructed from AACT <code>design_groups</code> + <code>interventions</code>: <strong>3 of 3</strong> pooled trials have a parser-confirmed contrast (the intervention of interest matched a differing coded arm). A trial with no registry arm data, or coded under a class label / development code we cannot machine-match, is shown as <em>contrast unverified</em> — a VISIBLE fail-open state, never silently treated as verified. <table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Contrast status</th><th>Randomised difference</th></tr><tr><td>30990260</td><td>parser-confirmed contrast</td><td title='parser-confirmed contrast: keyword &#x27;canagliflozin&#x27; matched AACT arm intervention &#x27;canagliflozin&#x27;; the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms'>canagliflozin</td></tr><tr><td>32970396</td><td>parser-confirmed contrast</td><td title='parser-confirmed contrast: keyword &#x27;dapagliflozin&#x27; matched AACT arm intervention &#x27;dapagliflozin&#x27;; the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms'>dapagliflozin</td></tr><tr><td>36331190</td><td>parser-confirmed contrast</td><td title='parser-confirmed contrast: keyword &#x27;empagliflozin&#x27; matched AACT arm intervention &#x27;empagliflozin&#x27;; the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms'>empagliflozin</td></tr></table></div><div class='absent'><strong>Funding / conflict-of-interest disclosure (per pooled trial, from source — disclosed, not adjusted).</strong> Industry-funded trials are a documented reporting-bias dimension (they tend to report more favourable results). For each pooled trial the funding source is classified from held text (full text preferred, abstract fallback) and the registry sponsor is shown as a second source when available; when held text and registry disagree, both source spans are rendered. Industry author affiliations are flagged only as affiliations, never sponsor evidence. Including an industry <em>drug-supply</em> tie in an otherwise independently funded trial: <strong>3 of 3 known</strong> (6 unknown) pooled trials are industry-funded or industry-tied (the industry-funded proportion of trials with KNOWN funding — unknown-funding trials are reported separately below, not counted as independently funded — for comparison against a comparator's). Absence is labelled by how deeply we looked — 0 with no funding statement in the <strong>full text</strong> (genuinely silent) and 0 where only the <strong>abstract</strong> was available (full text not retrieved) — so 'not stated' is never presented as 'independently funded'. The harness <strong>does not adjust</strong> for funding (the per-trial bias magnitude is not quantifiable from a funding line) — it is disclosed so a reader can weigh it. Never inferred.<table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Funding</th><th>Sponsors / roles</th><th>Scanned</th><th>Source evidence</th></tr><tr><td>PMID 32970396</td><td><strong>industry</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td>abstract</td><td><strong>abstract</strong>: (Funded by AstraZeneca; DAPA-CKD ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT03036150.).</td></tr><tr><td>PMID 30990260</td><td><strong>industry</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td>abstract</td><td><strong>abstract</strong>: (Funded by Janssen Research and Development; CREDENCE ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT02065791.).</td></tr><tr><td>PMID 36331190</td><td><strong>industry</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td>full text</td><td><strong>full text</strong>: (Funding:Boehringer Ingelheim, Eli Lilly and others; Clinicaltrials.gov:&lt;ext-link xmlns:xlink=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink&quot; ext-link-type=&quot;pmc:clinical-trial&quot; xlink:href=&quot;NCT03594110&quot;&gt;NCT03594110&lt;/ext-link&gt;, EuDRACT: 2017-002971-24).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/sec&gt;&lt;/abstract&gt;&lt;custom-meta-group&gt;&lt;custom-meta&gt;&lt;meta-name&gt;pmc-status-qastatus&lt;/meta-name&gt;&lt;meta-value&gt;0&lt;/meta-value&gt;&lt;/custom-meta&gt;&lt;custom-meta&gt;&lt;meta-name&gt;pmc-status-live&lt;/meta-name&gt;&lt;</td></tr><tr><td>NCT03190694</td><td><strong>source not retrieved</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td></td><td><strong></strong>: </td></tr><tr><td>NCT05570305</td><td><strong>source not retrieved</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td></td><td><strong></strong>: </td></tr><tr><td>NCT05614115</td><td><strong>source not retrieved</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td></td><td><strong></strong>: </td></tr><tr><td>NCT05735197</td><td><strong>source not retrieved</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td></td><td><strong></strong>: </td></tr><tr><td>NCT07060417</td><td><strong>source not retrieved</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td></td><td><strong></strong>: </td></tr><tr><td>NCT07344922</td><td><strong>source not retrieved</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td></td><td><strong></strong>: </td></tr></table></div><p><strong>Registry-machine-signal-restricted partial machine assessment</strong> (per pooled trial) &mdash; NOT a formal human risk-of-bias assessment, which requires human judgements the registry cannot supply. These are computed from what is machine-available (AACT 2026-08-30 + registry-vs-pooled (D5)). <strong>Domain 5 (selective reporting)</strong> is computed from the trial's REGISTERED primary outcome vs the outcome we pooled — a machine-checkable signal most published meta-analyses do not report. D1/D2/D4 use AACT structured allocation/masking fields. <strong>D3 (missing outcome data) is NOT ASSESSED for any trial — a stated limitation, not a per-trial judgement</strong>: the harness has no outcome-missingness evidence source (study discontinuation is not outcome missingness), so D3 is structurally unassessable here and is never rated; the attrition figures are shown as context only. This caps overall GRADE certainty below <em>high</em> corpus-wide (a