y; unextracted quantities and trial membership remain unknown.</p><p>HELD: cache/statins-primary-prevention-elderly/comparator_fulltext.txt; SHA-256 b6e274a0b1ee1784fa3c39a8f8f206be86540f09357707ad8c00bf20c2900634</p><dl><dt>k</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd><dt>effect</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd><dt>ci</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd><dt>i2</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd><dt>pi</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd><dt>method</dt><dd>NOT EXTRACTED from held text</dd></dl><p>Trial set NOT ENUMERATED; overlap unknown.</p></article></section><section class="tab" id="tab-riskofbias"><h3 class="tabname">Risk of bias</h3><p><strong>Coverage: 2 of 2 primary-outcome pooled trials assessed</strong> (1 from registry (AACT) + trial text, 1 from the abstract where AACT does not carry the trial)</p><div class='banner'><strong>RoB spans span-checked (cross-family): 97% agreement</strong> (32 of 33 scoreable), from a seeded sample of 45 model/registry-derived domain ratings independently checked by a different model family (Fable) against each trial abstract; 12 were unscoreable (no claim, or a conservative not-stated rating). This check itself found and fixed a real error &mdash; one trial (EMPHASIS-HF) was mislabelled NON_RANDOMIZED by the registry, contradicted by its abstract; the RoB block was also visibly broken until a human review caught it. The number is here because a RoB block a reader cannot trust is worthless (<code>docs/rob_spancheck.json</code>).</div><div class='absent'><strong>Parser-confirmed contrast disclosure (per pooled trial, from the AACT arm-label parser - disclosed, not an adjustment).</strong> This measures the parser, not the trial. Eligibility should test what actually DIFFERS between the randomised arms, not the mere presence of the drug word: a trial giving the drug of interest as BACKGROUND in every arm (e.g. all arms on the same agent, randomising a different drug) is not a randomised comparison of it. F