ase.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/fn&gt;&lt;fn id=&quot;t4fn2&quot;&gt;&lt;label&gt;†&lt;/label&gt;&lt;p&gt;One patient who died was intubated before receiving placebo and was excluded from the modified intention-to-treat population but included in the safety population.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/fn&gt;&lt;fn id=&quot;t4fn3&quot;&gt;&lt;label&gt;‡&lt;/label&gt;&lt;p&gt;Other events are listed in detail in Table S6.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/fn&gt;&lt;/table-wrap-foot&gt;&lt;/table-wrap&gt;<div class='ident'><em>endpoint binding:</em> binding: unbound_legacy; admissibility: UNBOUND_LEGACY</div><div class='xsrc'><em>consumer-consistency:</em> EXTRACTED_RECONSTRUCTION_WHILE_PUBLISHED_EXISTS - source span also reports an effect estimate with confidence interval; row keeps the existing reconstruction and is flagged for human review</div><div class='ident'><em>design key:</em> UNPROVEN / unit UNKNOWN; estimator RECONSTRUCTED; adjustment_status: UNRESOLVED (no located adjustment span); correlation handling none; action DESIGN_UNPROVEN <span class='muted'>PARALLEL</span></div><div class='ident'><em>compatibility row fields:</em> endpoint definition: primary outcome was intubation or death, assessed in a time-to-event analysis; follow-up window: 14 days; analysis set: modified intention-to-treat</div></td></tr><tr><td>40232661</td><td>PMID 40232661</td><td class='absent-cell'>HM: retrieved source reports harm in an incompatible structure</td><td>The abstract reports no serious adverse events, but the held safety analysis uses SOC 29 and tocilizumab 33 rather than the randomized 30 and 32, so an as-randomized safety denominator is not established.<br><code>POPULATION_MISMATCH</code><br><span class='muted'>reason-code audit: <code>REASON_FALSE_VALUE_HELD</code> fulltext:40232661: Fig. 2 Cumulative survival by treatment group Safety outcomes During the 28 days follow-up, 58 adverse events (AE) occurred in 27 participants (43.5%).</span><br><span class='muted'>span: &lt;table-wrap id=&quot;Tab3&quot; position=&quot;f